# a-base-behind-a-moat — BACKLOG C5, filled in by C9, and it is the
# THIRD of a triple.
#
# `a-base-nobody-builds.keys`, `a-base-the-player-builds.keys` and this
# file are the same file except for ONE token on one line:
#
#     paint off   →   nobody builds        falls at 130
#     paint on    →   a five-hex WALL      falls at 174   (`@M050`)
#     dig on      →   a five-hex TRENCH    falls at 221   (`@M059`)
#
# Same ground, same core, same spawn, same wave list, same crew, same
# drive, same number of ticks spent before the wave — so every
# difference below is the trench's and can be nothing else
# (`plans/12` § B7's rule).
#
# ── ⚠⚠ What C9 changed, and it is the whole reading ──────────────
#
# ⚠⚠ **This file used to say the base never fell: 378 ticks, still
# standing, on exactly the opening 200 points** (`@M058`).  A wave that
# cannot reach you cannot die, so the trench bought the whole run and
# earned nothing — time bought, income given up, all of it.
#
# **BACKLOG C9 fills it.**  A besieger stopped at a trench shovels it
# shut (`src/moat.loft` § What a besieger shovels), so the barrier is a
# TIMER: **+47 ticks over the wall the same ten helper-seconds a hex
# would have bought, and +91 over nothing.**  ⚠ The trench is a wall
# that cannot be UNBRACED — a fence presents 30 HP at its loose ends
# and a hole in the ground has no ends — which is what those 47 ticks
# are, priced.
#
# ── ⚠ What it still costs, and the scenario says all three ───────
#
#   1. **it earns nothing while it holds** — the wave stands at the far
#      bank digging, and nothing that cannot reach you dies, so the
#      wallet does not move until the wave is through.  ⚠ With a TOWER
#      behind it that stops being true, and it is the whole point:
#      `a-tower-behind-a-moat.keys` is the same trench with something
#      shooting across it;
#   2. ⚠⚠ **the crew dug themselves in** — they stood on the line to
#      work it, and a helper on finished water cannot leave.  ⚠ Since
#      C9 they cannot dig themselves out either: `salvage_at` refuses
#      SPOIL, because a clearer takes the whole pile whenever the pile
#      is smaller than one bite and one helper in reach would hold a
#      trench open for ever (`vehicle.loft` § SPOIL IS NOT SALVAGE).
#      What frees them is the wave finishing the job;
#   3. ⚠⚠ **and the player needs a BOOST to get back over it** — where
#      until BACKLOG C10 they could not get back at all.  The chassis
#      hovers (`@D006` closed), so the vehicle falls INTO a trench and
#      owes the metre back out, which 0.4 m of clearance has not and a
#      3.0 m boost has.  ⚠ `docs/PLAYING.md`'s *the only way out of a
#      base you have sealed* is therefore true of trenches as well as of
#      walls.  ⚠ The CREW have no boost, which is why (2) above is
#      unchanged.  Measured in `tests/c10_the_hover.loft` and
#      `a-trench-you-fall-into.keys` rather than here.

echo behind a moat: a trench drawn by driving, dug by the crew

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 11 0
marker 11 0 spawn 3

count markers 2 2
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -3 -2 12 -2
drag -3 -1 12 -1
drag -3 0 12 0
drag -3 1 12 1
drag -3 2 12 2
count painted 80 80

# The crew, sitting on the line the player is about to draw.
crew 5 -1
crew 5 1

# ── The dig ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
park 5 -2
dig on
drive 5 2
tick 6
count orders 5 5
dig off

# Park clear of the line so the trail is not rubbed out, and let the
# crew work.  A trench owes a wall's 10 s a hex — `build.loft`
# § BUILD_MOAT_UNITS chose that so the player's question is what it
# DOES rather than what it costs — so 50 helper-seconds over two
# helpers is 25 s, the same 45-tick window the wall version uses.
drive 0 0
tick 50
count orders 0 0
count painted 80 80
# ⚠⚠ The whole band, hex by hex — a barrier with ONE gap in it buys
# nothing at all (`plans/12` § B7 measured a gate at +1 tick), so
# *five* is the number that matters rather than *some*.
kind 5 -2 water
kind 5 -1 water
kind 5 0 water
kind 5 1 water
kind 5 2 water

# ⚠ The crew are in it.  They stood on the line to dig it and a helper
# on finished water cannot leave — the cost, stated where it happens.
helper 0 5 -1
helper 1 5 1


# ── The waves — identical to `an-undefended-base` ───────────────
wave 5
count alive 5 5

tick 22
wave 8
count alive 13 13

# ── The clock, and what it was bought with ──────────────────────
#
# ⚠⚠ **130 / 174 / 221 — the trench is worth +47 ticks over the wall
# the same price would have bought, and it is a TIMER rather than a
# wall nothing can break** (`@M059`).  The wave stops at the far bank,
# digs, and comes through what it dug.
fall 900
ticks 218 224

# ⚠⚠ **It earned NOTHING on the way**, which is the cost that survives
# C9: all thirteen are still alive when the base falls, because a wave
# standing at a trench is a wave nothing is shooting at.  That is the
# sentence `a-tower-behind-a-moat.keys` is the answer to.
count alive 13 13

# The line the wave came through, and the four it did not.  ⚠ It breaks
# where two besiegers happen to share a hex, so the reading is *one
# hex over the waterline and the rest under it* rather than a named
# row.
pile 5 1 1.0 2.0
pile 5 2 0.0 0.0

# ⚠ **The drive-east control lived HERE and has moved into
# `tests/c5_the_moat.loft` § What the probe killed** (`@DRY-129`).  It
# used to say *the player cannot follow the wave back across* by
# pointing the vehicle at the spawn after the run; that worked while the
# base never fell, and since C9 it falls with the wave standing on the
# core — so the vehicle is killed and RESPAWNED at (0, 0) mid-drive, and
# the reading became a fact about how many robots reached the core.
# ⚠⚠ **A control whose answer depends on something it is not about is
# not a control.**  ⚠ And the claim itself moved on again: BACKLOG C10
# gave the chassis its hover, so the vehicle now falls INTO a trench and
# BOOSTS out — `tests/c10_the_hover.loft` and
# `a-trench-you-fall-into.keys` are where that is measured.

snap c5_a_base_behind_a_moat
